  title: "The Acceptance Gate: Three Necessary Conditions for the Capacity to Act Against One's Strongest Schema"
  year: 2026
  notes: "Manuscript, in preparation for submission."
abstract: >-
  A minimal, dependency-free implementation of a three-condition model of
  autonomy: noticing a discrepancy, accepting it as true of oneself, and
  overriding the practised response. The conditions are combined
  multiplicatively, so each one caps the outcome and no surplus in the others
  lifts that cap. The worked cases from the accompanying manuscript are
  included as executable tests. Units are arbitrary and illustrative.
keywords:
  - metacognition
  - self-regulation
  - belief updating
  - self-worth
  - computational model
